\":\"# Venue notes\\n- Country: Australia (Sydney). Use region `au`.\\n- Genres: crowd loves film (the trivia master says so, and film scored best, about 65-90%). Music…\"},\"result\":\"Successfully wrote to memories/MEMORY.md\",\"error\":false}],\"plan\":\"That's all six rounds done. Here are the final standings:\\n\\n| Place | Team | Points |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Trivia Newton-John | 19 |\\n| 2 | The Bondi Brainstormers | 18 |\\n| 3 | Quizzly Bears | 16 |\\n| 4 | Les Quizerables | 13 |\\n| 5 | Opera House Party | 9 |\\n\\nRound by round, the share of answers the bank marked correct, and the difficulty I used:\\n1. **Film, difficulty 3:** 65%, so it stayed at 3.\\n2. **Music, difficulty 3:** 45%, so it dropped to 2.\\n3. **Film, difficulty 2:** 75%, so it stayed at 2, because the rule needs more than 75% to go up.\\n4. **Sport, difficulty 2:** 65%, so it stayed at 2.\\n5. **Film, difficulty 2:** 90%, so it went up to 3.\\n6. **Science, difficulty 3:** 35%.\\n\\nThe bank recorded the crowd's answers as each round was served, so I never submitted a sheet. I don't have the correct answers to read out. The marks above come from `round_summary`.\\n\\nI've saved notes for next week:\\n- **Country:** the venue is in Australia (region `au`).\\n- **Genres:** film is the crowd's strength. Music and science were hard for them.\\n- **Difficulty:** start next week at 2.\\n- **Not yet tried:** history and geography should get a turn.\\n\\nThe six short rounds were for tonight only, so I didn't save them as a lasting preference.\"}"
